[2026-01-30T14:13:24.139Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01AkXfhrS3vpaUFLyAJATA7m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017bU95Ho4mf6LcKsRw1i7AW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/direction1_content.md << 'DIRECTION_EOF'\n## Vision\nExtract common report generation logic into a declarative report builder that eliminates ~80% of duplicated code across 11 template files while maintaining full customization capability.\n\n## Business Value\n- Reduces template file sizes by 60-80% (current templates are 250-580 lines each)\n- New templates can be created in 50 lines instead of 400+\n- Bug fixes and improvements apply to all templates automatically\n- Easier to add new report variants (currently requires ~100 lines per variant)\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Create ReportBuilder base class with declarative section definitions\n- Extract common section rendering patterns (findings lists, extracted data formatting, markdown generation)\n- Implement section registry with configurable rendering strategies\n- Migrate one template as proof of concept\n\n**Excluded:**\n- Template configuration (FindingTypeConfig, TemplateConfig) - already well abstracted\n- Perspective and verification systems\n- Frontend/API changes\n\n## Key Components\n1. `ReportBuilder` class - Declarative report section definitions with rendering pipeline\n2. `SectionRenderer` protocol - Interface for custom section rendering (findings list, metrics table, timeline)\n3. `MarkdownBuilder` utility - Common markdown patterns (headers, tables, bullet lists with prefixes)\n4. Template migration - Update one template to use new system, validate output parity\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Analyze common patterns across `generate_*_report()` methods:\n   - Filter findings by type: `[f for f in findings if f.get(\"finding_type\") == \"X\"]`\n   - Extract structured data: `extracted = f.get(\"extracted_data\", {})`\n   - Format with optional prefix: `prefix = f\"**[{severity}]** \" if severity else \"\"`\n   - Build markdown sections with consistent structure\n\n2. Create declarative section specification:\n   ```python\n   @dataclass\n   class SectionSpec:\n       title: str\n       finding_types: List[str]\n       max_items: int = 5\n       extracted_fields: Optional[Dict[str, str]] = None  # field -> display format\n       show_severity: bool = False\n   ```\n\n3. Implement ReportBuilder with method:\n   ```python\n   def render_section(self, findings: List[Dict], spec: SectionSpec) -> str\n   ```\n\n4. Templates define sections declaratively:\n   ```python\n   risk_summary_sections = [\n       SectionSpec(\"Risk Assessment\", [\"red_flag\"], max_items=6, show_severity=True),\n       SectionSpec(\"Legal History\", [\"legal_history\"], max_items=5),\n   ]\n   ```\n\n## Files to Modify\n- `actor/src/templates/base.py` - Add ReportBuilder, SectionSpec, MarkdownBuilder classes\n- `actor/src/templates/due_diligence.py` - Migrate as first template (250 lines → ~80 lines)\n- All other templates after validation\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] Due diligence template migrated with identical output\n- [ ] Code reduction of 60%+ in migrated template\n- [ ] New report variant can be added with <20 lines of declarative config\n- [ ] No regression in report quality or format\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Extracted data schemas vary between templates - solved by optional field mapping\n- Some templates have unique formatting needs - solved by allowing custom renderer override\n- Output parity verification - create test cases comparing old vs new output\nDIRECTION_EOF"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":85879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f794eae-4516-40cc-88e2-7a8e0f0f09e3","uuid":"d9c315ba-346b-42e1-bdc7-6267207a2b44"}
